    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 5: Reading between the lines"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Good readers notice clues. Read this: Mia packed her bag the night before the trip. In the morning she woke early and ran to the window. Thick grey clouds covered the sky, but she grinned and pulled on her raincoat anyway. She could not wait to see the waterfalls."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "emoji": "🌧️",
      "alt": "Grey rainy clouds",
      "caption": "Grey clouds over Mia's trip"
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "How did Mia feel about the trip?",
        "ref": "c6",
        "skill_tag": "reading.inference",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "excited"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "bored"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "afraid"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "reveal",
      "prompt": "Which clues in the story tell you how Mia felt?",
      "answer_markdown": "She packed the night before, woke early, ran to the window and grinned even though it was cloudy. All of these clues show she was excited."
    },
